{
  "walkthrough": [
    "Goal: use OpenPaint in Chinese, my own language, or in English, and switch between them inside the app; every word I read is in the language I chose, and nothing else changes: my drawings, my brushes and my practice are the same in both.",
    "First start: my tablet's system language is Chinese, so OpenPaint opens in Chinese without asking: a blank canvas with 图库 at the top left, the islands' names in Chinese when the pen hovers over them. I draw a wave with the pen.",
    "Every panel reads in Chinese, in the same paper-white line art, at the same sizes: 操作 (添加, 分享, 画布, 触控笔, 语言 and the version line), the 笔按键 page, the brushes (笔刷: 最近, 素描, 上墨, 绘画, 纹理; 墨水笔, 勾线笔, 单线笔…) and the brush editor with its 大小动态 page, 图层 (图层 1, 不透明度, 正常, 正片叠底, 阿尔法锁定, 剪辑蒙版, 添加蒙版, 向下合并, 重命名…), 颜色 (色轮, 调色板), 调整 with 色相、饱和度、亮度, 选区 (手绘, 矩形, 反转, 取消选择), the copy menu (剪切, 拷贝, 拷贝全部, 复制, 剪切并粘贴, 粘贴), 变换 (水平翻转, 垂直翻转, 旋转 45°, 重置), notices and dialogs. Names the app gave read in Chinese too: 图层 1, 粘贴的图层, 未命名作品; a name I typed stays as I typed it.",
    "Switch: Actions, under 语言, shows English and 中文 each in its own words, 中文 in the ink pill. One tap on English: the whole interface reads in English at once, the panel still open, English in the pill. Undo does not touch it: it is a setting, kept with my brushes and colours, not a change to my artwork.",
    "Reopen: I leave the app and the system closes it; it opens again in English, the language I chose, not the system's. I switch back to 中文 and reopen: Chinese.",
    "Gallery in Chinese: 图库, the 今日 card (第 1 阶段 · 线条与颜色, 已完成 0 节，共约 15 节, 开始练习), my artwork's card titled 未命名作品, the 新建画布 popover (屏幕尺寸, 正方形, A4 竖向, A4 横向), a card's options (存为 OpenPaint 文件…, 版本), the delete question with 取消 and 删除, the rename dialog.",
    "Practice in Chinese, in V大's terms: the bar reads 线条 1/10, 怎么练, 叠图对比, 下一个; the card explains 单根线条 in our own words with 草稿笔, 画线笔 and 修正笔; 叠图对比 lays the original over my copy 原位 or 对齐; a colour (单色) compares as 更红/更黄, 更亮/更暗, 更纯/更灰 with 色相, 饱和度, 明度; the summary reads 第 1 节完成.",
    "Nothing else changes with the language: the strokes and fills are the same pixels (the checkpoints are English runs' hashes), and the controls keep their English names, so every scenario, bench and device chore names them alike in both."
  ],
